## 3. How the System Works — Without the Technical Language

Think of UBS-LMIS as a **three-layer building**:

**The Foundation (Backend / Brain)**
This is the engine running behind the scenes. It stores all data in a secure, structured database — student records, fee invoices, attendance logs, assessment scores, and payroll data. It enforces rules: a teacher cannot take attendance for a class they don't teach. An accountant cannot see another school's data. A student cannot see another student's results.

**The Middleware (Security Layer)**
Every user logs in with a unique username and password. The system issues a digital "key" (called a JWT token) that expires automatically. If someone loses their phone or laptop, their session is not permanently exposed. All passwords are encrypted using industry-standard cryptography — even the database administrator cannot read them.

**The Interface (The Portal)**
This is the website every user visits. It looks different depending on who you are. The Head of School sees charts and dashboards. The teacher sees their class register. The student sees their results. It is responsive — it works on a ₵800 phone as well as a laptop.

