## 4. Why This is Industry Grade

This section answers the question your most technical board member might ask: *"Is this the real thing, or is this a student project?"*

### 🔐 Security
- Every route in the system is **role-protected**. You cannot reach any data without logging in first.
- The system uses **method-level security checks** — even if a URL is guessed, the server checks permissions before returning any data.
- Passwords are hashed with **Argon2id** — the same standard used by banks and financial institutions.
- All tokens expire. Sessions cannot be hijacked long-term.

### ☁️ Cloud Architecture
- The system is deployed on **Render** — the same class of cloud infrastructure used by startups and mid-sized tech companies globally.
- The database is a **managed PostgreSQL 16 instance** — enterprise-grade, automatically backed up.
- The application runs in a **Docker container** — portable, reproducible, and consistent across any environment.
- Cold start times on the free tier have been specifically engineered around: the login endpoint uses a **4-minute timeout** to compensate for platform sleep states, so users are never left staring at a broken screen.

### 📊 Data Integrity
- The database uses **Flyway migrations** — every structural change to the database is versioned, tracked, and repeatable. There are 25 ordered migration scripts that define the entire schema.
- All primary keys are **UUIDv7** — time-ordered unique identifiers that are optimised for database indexing performance. This matters as the student count grows to thousands.
- **Audit trails** on every record: the system automatically records *who* created or modified any record, and *when*.

### 🔄 Resilience
- The JWT system uses **two tokens** (access + refresh). If a user's session expires mid-use, the system silently refreshes it without logging them out. The user never notices.
- All API errors return standardised, traceable error codes (RFC 7807 format) with unique trace IDs — if something goes wrong, the exact error can be found in logs immediately.

### 🧩 Architecture
- The backend is a **Modular Monolith** — 16 distinct business modules (academics, finance, attendance, assessment, communication, progression, payroll, etc.), each self-contained. This means the system can scale, and any module can be independently updated or extended without breaking the others.
- The frontend is built on **Next.js 14** — the same framework used by companies like TikTok, Twitch, and Hulu for their web interfaces.

